{"term":{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000253","compactId":"SO_0000253","id":"SO:0000253","label":"tRNA","definition":{"text":"Transfer RNA (tRNA) molecules are approximately 80 nucleotides in length. Their secondary structure includes four short double-helical elements and three loops (D, anti-codon, and T loops). Further hydrogen bonds mediate the characteristic L-shaped molecular structure. Transfer RNAs have two regions of fundamental functional importance: the anti-codon, which is responsible for specific mRNA codon recognition, and the 3' end, to which the tRNA's corresponding amino acid is attached (by aminoacyl-tRNA synthetases). Transfer RNAs cope with the degeneracy of the genetic code in two manners: having more than one tRNA (with a specific anti-codon) for a particular amino acid; and 'wobble' base-pairing, i.e. permitting non-standard base-pairing at the 3rd anti-codon position.","xrefs":["ISBN:0198506732","http://www.sanger.ac.uk/cgi-bin/Rfam/getacc?RF00005"]},"comments":["This term is mapped to MGED. Do not obsolete without consulting MGED ontology."],"synonyms":[{"scope":"exact","value":"INSDC_feature:tRNA"},{"scope":"related","value":"transfer RNA"},{"scope":"related","value":"transfer ribonucleic acid"},{"scope":"broad","value":"INSDC_qualifier:unknown"}],"xrefs":["http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TRNA"],"subsets":["SOFA"],"altIds":[],"namespace":"sequence","isObsolete":false,"replacedBy":[],"canonicalUrl":"/browser/current_release/term/SO:0000253/","history":{"firstSeen":{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files"},"mostRecent":{"hash":"37bb439ab106ce016dbe5c1125c8f6d112b8888f","shortHash":"37bb439","date":"2020-05-13","subject":"Added term sncRNA SO:0002247 in response to GitHub Issue #485"},"entries":[{"hash":"37bb439ab106ce016dbe5c1125c8f6d112b8888f","shortHash":"37bb439","date":"2020-05-13","subject":"Added term sncRNA SO:0002247 in response to GitHub Is